Z||000000||Galen||06-03-2001||08:41 PM||||before I start I must state a disclaimer as advised by me. The following statement(s) are solely the opinion(s) of me, they may or may not reflect the opinion(s) of this forum or any of its other members. If you wish to complain or threaten me with a lawsuit. Please, go find a tree and talk to it. I do not wish to hear it. Thank you very much. And now, on to the show.<P>I've noticed lately that people have been getting unruley about what other people have said. I however have not really felt like bothering myself to read into it all so my opinions may biased towards peope I respect & like. is it slanderous for me to say "the FieroStore sucks becuz they have high prices"? It is true that they have high prices, and that in my opinion sucks. If I said, "Dont shop at the Fiero Store becuz they have high prices". Is that sladerous? Merely a suggestion, I am not forcing anyone away from shopping at the fiero store. In my own protection, the Fiero Store does have high prices, and that sucks. But shop thee  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe.<P>Let me jump to another subject, still sticking with the legal action BS. the statement I made the other day ... "We can settle this in other ways" ... Let me explain some of the other ways, We could go out to a field and compare units, like  I suggested to Songman(to whom I do respect and consider a friend). Or perhaps a streetrace(arn't I gonna get flamed for that one). Maybe we could play a game of cards? Or arm wrestle? One certian forum members response to that statement shows exactly what is wrong with this world today. People put too much into too little. This is a public forum, lets have some public fun without people trying to intemidate others with stupid and childish threats. <P>the preceeding thread is brought to you by Galen, Whenever you need someone to talk to, talk to Galen  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe, sorry for the rant.<P>----------